---
import LegalPage from "../../components/LegalPage.astro";
import {
  keepAfterStopPaying,
  minimumAge,
  notAffiliated,
  operator,
  paymentProvider,
} from "../../content/legal";

---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The rules for using DMbot: plans, recording, what DMbot does and doesn't do, and ending your account."
  heading="Terms of use"
  summary="DMbot listens to your game in Discord and quietly helps the game master (DM). It only records people who said yes, and everyone in the server can read what it writes down. You keep what you make and let DMbot use it to run and improve DMbot; you can turn the improving off in My Account. DMbot gives advice; the game master decides. It can mishear and make mistakes, so check anything important. Plans are paid monthly through our payment company, and you can change or stop any time. Don't use DMbot to record people who haven't agreed, and only share books or adventures you have the right to use."
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    DMbot is run by {operator.name} ("we"). Write to {operator.email}. By adding DMbot to a server or
    signing in, you agree to these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can use DMbot</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You must be at least {minimumAge}, and follow Discord's own rules.
    </li>
    <li>
      The person who adds DMbot to a server, or runs a campaign, is responsible for using it
      fairly in that server.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Recording and saying yes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      DMbot records only people who said yes (the "I consent" button or
      <code>/consent give</code>). Anyone can stop at any time: press 🗂️ Menu in DMbot's
      private message to you, then "Stop recording me", then "Yes". Or type
      <code>/consent revoke</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      What DMbot writes down can be read by everyone in that Discord server, and downloaded on
      paid plans.
    </li>
    <li>
      Don't try to record people who haven't agreed, for example by playing their voice through
      someone else's microphone.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What DMbot does, and doesn't</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      DMbot gives the game master quiet advice. It never makes up story and never decides. The
      game master decides.
    </li>
    <li>
      DMbot can mishear words, mix up names, and get rules wrong. Every rules tip shows where it
      comes from and how sure DMbot is. Check anything that matters.
    </li>
    <li>
      We work hard to keep DMbot running, but we can't promise it never stops or never loses a
      line. DMbot is provided as is, with no promise it will always be available.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Plans and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Plans, prices and hours are on the <a href="/pricing">Prices</a> page. Paid plans renew
      every month until you stop them. Try It never turns into a paid plan by itself, and it needs no payment details. To keep
      going after Try It, pick a plan.
    </li>
    <li>
      Payments are taken by {paymentProvider}, who is the seller. Their terms apply to the
      payment, and they add any sales tax.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can change or stop your plan any time from <a href="/account">My Account</a>. A stopped
      plan keeps working until the end of the period you already paid for.
    </li>
    <li>
      If a renewal payment fails, there is a short grace period to fix it before the plan stops.
      Tap Fix my payment in <a href="/account">My Account</a>. If your first payment doesn't go
      through, the plan doesn't start until it does. If the plan stops, campaigns are
      kept for {keepAfterStopPaying}, then deleted.
    </li>
    <li>Refunds are explained on the <a href="/legal/refunds">Refunds</a> page.</li>
    <li>
      Prices may change at any time. The price shown when you buy is the price you pay for
      that period.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your campaign and your words</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You keep what you and your table make. Your campaign, notes and what your table says belong
      to you and your table, not to us. You give DMbot a worldwide, royalty-free licence to store,
      process and show them, to run DMbot and to improve it (you can turn the improving off in My Account). Within the table, the game masters run
      the campaign. Only the game master whose plan it uses can delete it (for a free campaign,
      the one who started it).
    </li>
    <li>
      When a game master shares an adventure or a rulebook, they confirm they have the right to
      use it. We don't check this and give no legal advice. It stays in that one campaign, and the
      game master can delete it.
    </li>
    <li>
      What DMbot makes from a session belongs to the campaign, and is deleted only with the
      campaign. That means a recap, story facts, notes for the game master, and anything else
      DMbot writes from what was said.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you stop being recorded, take back your yes or delete your account, DMbot stops
      recording you and removes what the <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy page</a> says it
      removes. You can ask for your own lines and what DMbot learned about you to be deleted, as
      far as they can be separated from the rest: press 🗂️ Menu in DMbot's private message to you,
      then Delete my transcripts or "Stop recording me", or delete your account. Lines you said in
      other people's campaigns are removed only by Delete my transcripts: deleting your account
      does not remove them. What DMbot already made from sessions you took part in stays with
      the campaign, and so do copies other people downloaded. Only deleting the campaign removes
      what DMbot made, and only the game master whose plan the campaign uses can delete it. If
      we can't delete something, it stays, and everything else you asked for still happens.
    </li>
    <li>
      If someone tells us shared material breaks their rights, we may remove it.
      Write to {operator.email} with a link to the material.
    </li>
    <li>
      Backups of a paid campaign hold the campaign, including the game master's secrets.
      Anyone in the server may download one. Whoever loads a backup becomes the game master of
      that copy.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Fair use</h2>
  <p>
    Don't use DMbot to break the law, to harass anyone, to share content Discord doesn't allow,
    or to get around plan limits. Don't try to break into DMbot or other people's campaigns. We
    may pause or close an account that does this.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You can delete your account any time from <a href="/account">My Account</a>.
      Deleting removes your sign-in details and ends your plan at once; you won't be charged
      again, and the rest of the month isn't paid back. If you want money back, ask before you
      delete (see <a href="/legal/refunds#stopping">Refunds</a>). Your campaigns are not deleted
      with your account, because the other players may still want to read or download them.
      They are deleted 120 days later, unless another DM of the campaign takes them over. If the
      owner's Discord account is gone, or the owner has been out of the server for 7 days, DMbot
      offers the campaign's other game masters a button to take the campaign on. Only a game
      master who presses it takes over.
    </li>
    <li>
      We may stop offering DMbot. If we do, we'll give paid users at least 30 days'
      notice and time to download their backups.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    {operator.name}, its affiliates and any contributors to the DMbot project make no claims or
    promises towards the accuracy or stability of the product's performance. {operator.name} does
    not warrant or guarantee the goods or services purchased. By using the DMbot agent and the
    associated tools, users agree to hold {operator.name} and its affiliates harmless towards
    any losses, material, non-material or deemed.
  </p>

  <h2>Not connected to the game's publisher</h2>
  <p>{notAffiliated}</p>
  <p>The background artwork was made with Gemini and Claude, from our own prompts.</p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    If we change these terms, we'll update this page and tell signed-in users before the change
    starts. If the question people say yes to changes, DMbot asks everyone again before it records them.
  </p>

  <h2>The law that applies</h2>
  <p>
    The laws of the State of Ohio, USA, apply to these terms, and any dispute about them is heard
    in the courts of the State of Ohio, USA.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
